1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,743
The numbers hid a bitter riddle: an impressive gain that consisted entirely of one good month.

2
00:00:05,743 --> 00:00:10,997
“Therefore the trend is an insult to the reader,” the auditor said.

3
00:00:10,997 --> 00:00:19,916
“A symbolic pat on the back is not a systematic check, and an exact figure can still be a sour one.”

4
00:00:19,916 --> 00:00:24,486
The behavioral evidence was audio, and it was loud.

5
00:00:24,486 --> 00:00:32,405
“Consequently, an ambition devoted to a single quarter will necessarily wander,” Maya wrote.

6
00:00:32,405 --> 00:00:44,709
“The implement we need is a precautionary one, not a stylish one.” Soon the council would knock and ask for the perfect version of the same page.

7
00:00:44,709 --> 00:00:50,443
The acceptable range was narrow and the excuse for missing it was not rational.

8
00:00:50,443 --> 00:00:56,427
“A dent in the record is a clue, not a crime,” the director said.

9
00:00:56,427 --> 00:01:02,597
“Be straightforward about the assumption and the reader will forgive the rest.”

10
00:01:02,597 --> 00:01:06,511
The irrational part was the vanity of the author.

11
00:01:06,511 --> 00:01:13,056
“A juicy quote and a silky paragraph will not make a dent disappear,” Lin said.

12
00:01:13,056 --> 00:01:21,855
“A dependable number is worth more than a reflective one, and both are worth more than a swipe at the opposition.”

13
00:01:21,855 --> 00:01:28,189
The resolute answer was to publish the desertion figures alongside the growth figures.

14
00:01:28,189 --> 00:01:33,658
“These are the same room and the same simple choice,” the auditor said.

15
00:01:33,658 --> 00:01:41,557
“We can suggest that the low quarter was seasonal, and we cannot pretend that it did not occur.”

16
00:01:41,557 --> 00:01:49,847
The choosy reader would want the whole series, and the whole series was now required by the term of the contract.

17
00:01:49,847 --> 00:01:55,471
The numbers would hide nothing, and the group would have to live with what they showed.

18
00:01:55,471 --> 00:02:06,300
Therefore the hard number arrived soon, and it was not perfect: the series consisted necessarily of one loud knock and one quiet scream.

19
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:15,258
Consequently, we must wander through every acceptable implement and comprise the exact clue in the straightforward line.

20
00:02:15,258 --> 00:02:24,037
A bitter ambition devoted to a rational story is still irrational, and a pat on the back is not a behavioral finding.

21
00:02:24,037 --> 00:02:27,852
The chance to require a better figure is now.

22
00:02:27,852 --> 00:02:37,261
A stylish and juicy vanity is not a dependable swipe, and the excitement of the entire series must be checked systematically.

23
00:02:37,261 --> 00:02:41,360
We intend to test the feeling of the reader as well.

24
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:48,449
Whom shall we ask, and whose name stands on the page, and is the number good yet?

25
00:02:48,449 --> 00:02:53,510
The reader would seem to want the whole series.
